{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"117639","commit":"1cf496e3184f9655d8360db1c464f1d40b2c8c95","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The output column ordering for LEFT joins changes significantly. The old code produced: `leftOutput` first, then `rightOutput` (with right overriding on name conflicts). The new code produces: `rightOutput` (minus match fields) first, then `leftOutput` (with left overriding on name conflicts).\nFor example, with `left \u003d [id, a, b]` and `right \u003d [id, c, d]`:\n- Old result: `[right.id, left.a, left.b, right.c, right.d]`\n- New result: `[right.c, right.d, left.id, left.a, left.b]`\nThis is a behavioral change in column ordering that could break any consumer (tests, downstream plan nodes, or user-facing column positions) that relied on the previous \"left-first\" ordering. If this reordering is intentional, it would be worth a brief note in the commit message or a comment explaining the new ordering rationale.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-30311:30407,30420:30531,31780:31843,31860:31938,31955:32033,32051:32115,32132:32178,32219:32223,32345:32351-30245:30342,31616:31624","promptId":"#CF847","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":30311,"endPos":30407,"startLine":612,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":612,"endLineOffset":108,"length":97},{"pos":30420,"endPos":30531,"startLine":613,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":613,"endLineOffset":123,"length":112},{"pos":31780,"endPos":31843,"startLine":635,"startLineOffset":16,"endLine":635,"endLineOffset":79,"length":64},{"pos":31860,"endPos":31938,"startLine":636,"startLineOffset":16,"endLine":636,"endLineOffset":94,"length":79},{"pos":31955,"endPos":32033